      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes requested** — See inline comments for details. [[trajectory](go/traj/24d090b1-8194-4361-8ea1-b5396c87edaf)]\n\n### Review Summary\n**Functionality**: ❌ The integer wrap-around vulnerability this patch aims to fix does not exist. The `offset` parameter is already bounded by `validate_fp_buffer_offset` on line 623 to be less than or equal to `sizeof(fp_buffer)`. Because of this prior validation, it is mathematically impossible for `offset + FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_OFFSET` to wrap around `UINT32_MAX`. The newly added check is therefore dead code. The added regression test passes only because `validate_fp_buffer_offset` rejects the large offset before the new check is even evaluated.\n**Security**: ✅ No new security vulnerabilities introduced. The existing bounds checking (`validate_fp_buffer_offset` and the subsequent bounds check after adding the image offset) correctly prevent out-of-bounds reads.\n**Style**: ✅ The code is clean and adheres to style guidelines.\n**Testing**: ✅ A new regression test was added. While it tests the correct behavior (an error is returned), this rejection is handled by the existing validation logic. The test is still valuable as a regression test for `validate_fp_buffer_offset` itself.\n**Overall Quality**: The patch adds redundant code to address an impossible condition. I recommend dropping the redundant check in `fpsensor.cc` and keeping the test, potentially rewording its comments to reflect that it exercises `validate_fp_buffer_offset`.",
